API:
  - Fold every Worker route under /api/* (/api/search, /api/ingest/rating, ...) so the Pages proxy forwards paths unchanged and the agent's CLOUDFLARE_API_BASE_URL gets /api appended. Keep /api/ingest/* out of the proxy allowlist. Deploy the worker and agent together; update tests, README and functions/api/[[path]].ts

Hygience:
  - Upgrade to latest version

Performance, Worker CPU (context: the free plan allows 10 ms CPU per invocation; over the 30 days to 2026-11-09, pixdex-worker p50 was 1.7 ms, p99 27 ms, and 242 requests ended as exceededResources, so Workers Paid is currently masking this):
  - Measure first: run `wrangler tail pixdex-worker --format json` during an indexing batch, a person match and a groups load, and record cpuTime per route. Static analysis only; no route is confirmed yet. Re-check with the GraphQL workersInvocationsAdaptive quantiles (cpuTimeP99) after each fix

Performance, D1 (from `wrangler d1 insights pixdex --timePeriod 30d`: about 21.5M rows read, 70K written, measured before the albums table and counters shipped; re-run it to see what is left):
  - Photos list `SELECT photos.* ... ORDER BY last_indexed DESC LIMIT ? OFFSET ?` (562 runs; idx_photos_last_indexed now serves it, so deep pages still cost offset + limit rows)
    - Switch from OFFSET (the UI uses page numbers and offsets, so keyset changes the API and the pager) to keyset pagination (cursor = last_indexed + id); update the frontend cursor handling and tests
  - People cover/ROW_NUMBER() PARTITION BY f.person_id query (195 runs, about 5.4K rows): store the chosen cover face on persons (persons.cover_face_id exists) and update it when faces are confirmed or unassigned or the cover changes
  - Filtered searches (q, album, dates, people) still run COUNT(*) on every request; cache or skip it on non-first pages if it shows up in the top 5
  - Re-check after the above: face matching scan `faces WHERE det_score >= 0.7 ... rowid > ?` (260 runs, about 3.6K rows, efficiency 0.05) and `faces WHERE id IN (json_each(?))` (1,509 runs, about 1K rows). Both look acceptable (paged by rowid / primary-key lookups); only act if they stay in the top 5
  - Add a note to docs/development.md on how to re-run `wrangler d1 insights` and the CPU GraphQL query, and re-run both after each change to confirm the drop
